The bloodline of Christ.
This is a record of the lineage of Jesus Christ. He is the son of David. He is also the son of Abram.
Abraham was the father of Isaac. And Isaac was the father of Jacob. And Jacob was the father of Judah and his brothers.
Yehuda is the father of Perez and Zira. Tamar was their mother. Perez is the father of Hezron. Hezron is the father of Ram.
Ram was the father of Amminadab. Amminadab was the father of Nahshon. Nahshon was the father of Salmon.
Boaz was the father of Obed. Ruth was the mother of Obed. Obed was the father of Jesse.
Jesus was the father of king David, and David was the father of Solomon, and Solomon's mother was Uriah's wife.
Solomon was the father of Rehoboam. And Rehoboam was the father of Abijah. And Abijah was the father of Asa.
Asa was the father of Jehoshaphat. And Jehoshaphat was the father of Joram. And Joram was the father of Uzziah.
Uzziah was the father of Ahaz. Ahaz was the father of Hezekiah.
Structurally, Manasseh was the father of Amon, Amon was the father of Josiah.
Yosef was the father of Yekoniah and his brother. At that time, the Jewish people were forced to leave Babylon.
After that, the family line continued. Jechoniah was the father of Shealtiel. And Shealtiel was the father of Zorubbabel.
Zerubbabel is the father of Abiud. Abiud is the father of Eliakim. Eliakim is the father of Azor.
Azor was the father of Zadok. Zadok was the father of Akim. Akim was the father of Eliud.
Alyaud was the father of Elieazar. And Elieazar was the father of Mathan. And Mathan was the father of Jacob.
Jacob was the father of Joseph; and Joseph was the husband of Mary; and Mary gave birth to Jesus, who is called Christ.
So, there were 14 generations from Abram to David, then 14 generations from David until the Jewish people were forced to leave it for Babylon, then 14 generations from that time to Christ. Christ Jesus was born.
Thus Jesus Christ was born. He knew that Mary and Joseph had agreed to marry. But before they began to live together, it became clear that Mary would become pregnant. And she was conceived by the power of the Holy Spirit.
Her husband Yoshi was a man of faith. He did not want to openly mislead her. So he planned to secretly divorce her.
But as he was thinking about this, an angel of God's grace appeared to him in a dream. And the angel said, "Joseph, son of David, do not be afraid to take Mary as your wife. The child within her is from the Holy Spirit."
He will be born a son. You must name him Jesus. This is because he will save his people from their sins.
