The wise men visit Jesus.
Jesus was born in Bethlehem of Judea. This happened while Herod was king of Judea. After Jesus was born, wise men from the east came to Jerusalem.
They asked, "Where is the child who was born to be king of the Jews? For we saw his star when it rose and have come to worship him."
When King Herod heard this, he was deeply disturbed, and all in Jerusalem were terrified.
Therefore Herod called together all the chief priests of the people, and the teachers of the law, and asked them where the Christ was to be born.
