Jesus replied, "My sister, you have great faith! Your request will be granted." And the woman's daughter was healed at that very moment. Jesus Feeds the Four Thousand
Jesus went out from there. He walked on the lake of Galilee. Then he went up on a mountain and sat down.
Large crowds came to him, and they brought people who were lame, blind, crippled, mute, and many others. They laid them down at his feet, and he healed them.
People were astonished. For those who could not speak began to speak. The sick were healed. Those who could not walk began to walk. Those who were blind began to see. So people were giving thanks to God who is called in Israel.
Jesus took his servant and instructed them to listen. He said: "I deserve the credit for these people. They brought me for three days. They had nothing to be happy about. I did not want to send them away hurriedly. If I send them away, they will be weak on their way to their home."
His servants answered him, "Nothing is here," and they said, "Where can we get enough bread to satisfy this huge crowd?"
