Jesus went into the region of Caesarea Philippi. His disciples asked him, "What do people say about the Son of Man?"
They answered: "Some say that it is John the Baptist, others say that it is Elijah, others say that it is Jeremiah, or one of the prophets."
"But what about you?" he asked. "Who do you say that I am?"
Simon Peter answered and said, "You are the Christ, the Son of the living God."
Jesus answered, "Blessed are you, Simon, son of Jonah! For flesh and blood has not revealed this to you, but My Father who is in heaven.
Here is what I tell you. You are Peter. I will build my church on this rock. And the gates of hell will not be able to destroy it.
I will give you the keys to the kingdom of heaven. Whatever you bind on earth will be bound in heaven. And whatever you loose on earth will be loosed in heaven.
Then Jesus told his servants not to tell anyone that he was the Christ. Jesus speaks about his coming for death.
From that time on, Jesus began explaining to his disciples what was going to happen to him. He told them that he must go to Jerusalem, where he would be betrayed into the hands of the chief priests and the teachers of the law. He would be condemned and handed over to the Gentiles, who would mock him, scourge him, and finally kill him by crucifixion. But on the third day, he would rise from the dead.
Peter took Jesus aside and began to rebuke him. "No, Lord!" Peter said. "This will never happen to you!"
Jesus took his face, and said to Peter: "Slip behind me, Satan! You are taking the rise of my course. But you are not keeping what is emanating from God, but you are keeping what is emanating from man."
Jesus took his servants and said, "If anyone wishes to come after me, he must deny himself and take up his cross, and follow me."
If he wants to save his life, he will lose it. But if he loses his life for me, he will find it.
What good is it for someone to own the whole world but lose their soul? Or what could someone possibly exchange for their soul?
The Son of Man will come in the glory of His Father. His angels will come with Him, and He will reward each person according to what they have done.
What I am going to tell you is the truth. Some of those standing here will not taste death before they see the Son of Man coming in his kingdom.
Changes the appearance of Jesus
After six days, Jesus took Peter, James, and John, the brother of James, with him, and went up with them to a high mountain. They were all alone.
And his appearance changed before them. His face was shining like the sun. His clothes became white like light.
At that moment, Moses and Elijah appeared before them in a glorious manifestation. Moses and Elijah were talking with Jesus.
Peter said to Jesus, "Lord, it is good for us to be here. If you wish, I will put up three tabernacles; one for you, one for Moses, and one for Elijah."
While Peter was speaking, a cloud of light appeared around them. And the voice from the cloud said, "This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased. Listen to him!"
When the Muslims heard this, they trembled and fell down on their heads.
But Jesus came and stood in their midst. He said, "Peace be with you; do not be afraid."
When they looked up, they saw no one but Jesus.
They came from the mountain. And on the way back, Jesus told them what to do: "Do not tell anyone what you have seen," and he said, "Wait until the Son of Man is raised from the dead."
The teachers asked them: "Why do the teachers say that Elijah must be sent first?"
Jesus answered, "Yes, Elijah must come first to make everything new again."
But I tell you, Elijah has come already. But the people did not recognize him, and they did to him everything they wanted to do. In the same way, the Son of Man will be treated.
